.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 

.PP
.nf
Implements the low-level algorithms Sphinx uses for versioning doctrees\&.
.fi
.PP
 
.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS " Iterator[\fBNode\fP] sphinx\&.versioning\&.add_uids (\fBNode\fP doctree, Callable[[\fBNode\fP], bool] condition)"

.PP
.nf
Add a unique id to every node in the `doctree` which matches the
condition and yield the nodes\&.

:param doctree:
    A :class:`docutils\&.nodes\&.document` instance\&.

:param condition:
    A callable which returns either ``True`` or ``False`` for a given node\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SS " float sphinx\&.versioning\&.get_ratio (str old, str new)"

.PP
.nf
Return a 'similarity ratio' (in percent) representing the similarity
between the two strings where 0 is equal and anything above less than equal\&.

.fi
.PP
 
.SS " int sphinx\&.versioning\&.levenshtein_distance (str a, str b)"

.PP
.nf
Return the Levenshtein edit distance between two strings *a* and *b*\&.
.fi
.PP
 
.SS " Iterator[\fBNode\fP] sphinx\&.versioning\&.merge_doctrees (\fBNode\fP old, \fBNode\fP new, Callable[[\fBNode\fP], bool]
 condition)"

.PP
.nf
Merge the `old` doctree with the `new` one while looking at nodes
matching the `condition`\&.

Each node which replaces another one or has been added to the `new` doctree
will be yielded\&.

:param condition:
    A callable which returns either ``True`` or ``False`` for a given node\&.

.fi
.PP
 
